# Cron jobs.
#
# THIS IS A TEMPLATE. Do not edit the installed crontab on the server, and do
# not edit this file on the server either: deploy/deploy.sh renders it
# (swapping __SITE_URL__ for the site's address and __HEARTBEAT__ for an
# optional outside ping) and pipes it through `crontab -` on every deploy, so
# any hand edit is silently overwritten on the next release. Change it here,
# in the repository, and release.
#
# The site is files and a proxy, so there is little to schedule. Every line
# carries the reason for its interval.

MAILTO=""
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# The site answers over HTTPS with a page, end to end through DNS, the
# certificate and Caddy. Every five minutes because it is what pings the
# heartbeat: the outside service alerts when the pings stop. Without
# HEARTBEAT_URL it still runs, and does nothing anyone sees.
*/5 * * * * curl -fsS -m 20 -o /dev/null __SITE_URL__/ >/dev/null 2>&1__HEARTBEAT__
